# WireGuard tunnel between the observation server 119 and the hypervisor 66 (T and S testbeds).
# Source of truth for addresses: docs/spec-testbed-vm-3tier.md §3-1, §3-4 and
# docs/spec-testbed-sms-only.md §3-2, §3-5. No key material here: keys are made on each host.
# Every value can be overridden from the environment of the caller.

WG_IF=${WG_IF:-wg0}
WG_MTU=${WG_MTU:-1420}
WG_PREFIX=${WG_PREFIX:-30}
WG_ADDR_119=${WG_ADDR_119:-10.250.0.1}
WG_ADDR_66=${WG_ADDR_66:-10.250.0.2}
WG_HOST_119=${WG_HOST_119:-192.168.230.119}
WG_HOST_66=${WG_HOST_66:-192.168.200.66}
WG_KEEPALIVE=${WG_KEEPALIVE:-25}

# UDP ports tried in this order when the port is not given (decision 8 (a)). None of them is a
# port 119 listens on (11-16 read: 8472, 53 on loopback, 514).
WG_PORT_CANDIDATES=${WG_PORT_CANDIDATES:-"51820 51821 4500 1194 443"}

# Networks routed through the tunnel. T: uplink 123 and the web, WAS, DB networks 124~126.
# The S business network (192.168.131.0/24) is added later with "add-net", at ST2.
WG_NETS_DEFAULT=${WG_NETS_DEFAULT:-"192.168.123.0/24 192.168.124.0/24 192.168.125.0/24 192.168.126.0/24"}

# Networks that must never ride the tunnel: the existing testbed, the management and user
# networks of T and S, the office networks and the worker VLAN.
WG_DENY_NETS=${WG_DENY_NETS:-"192.168.122.0/24 192.168.127.0/24 192.168.132.0/24 192.168.133.0/24 192.168.200.0/24 192.168.213.0/24 192.168.230.0/24"}

# What the tunnel may open on 119, by original destination 10.250.0.1:<port>. Agent reports
# (18090), syslog (514 udp and tcp), traps (162). Echo requests to 10.250.0.1 and replies to
# flows 119 started (SNMP polls, pings) are always allowed. Anything else from the tunnel is
# dropped, so the testbed VMs cannot reach 119 NodePorts, hostPorts or host services.
WG_IN_TCP_119=${WG_IN_TCP_119:-"18090 514"}
WG_IN_UDP_119=${WG_IN_UDP_119:-"514 162"}

# Health limits (spec §6-4 preflight, §10 T0).
WG_HANDSHAKE_MAX=${WG_HANDSHAKE_MAX:-150}
WG_RTT_EXTRA_MS=${WG_RTT_EXTRA_MS:-2}
WG_RTT_MAX_MS=${WG_RTT_MAX_MS:-20}
WG_CONNTRACK_MAX_RATIO=${WG_CONNTRACK_MAX_RATIO:-80}

# The 119 pod whose network namespace is used to prove the collector side reaches the tunnel.
WG_POD_NAME=${WG_POD_NAME:-collector-nms}
# A port nobody listens on: a refused connection proves the TCP path both ways and starts no
# service on the far side (no log line on 66 that its syslog would carry to 119).
WG_POD_TCP_PORT=${WG_POD_TCP_PORT:-9}
